	(text "Gate lines: 1 k to ground at the label, 1 k in series\nat the driver input. Without the controller every\nswitch is open; a line that is high without +12V_A\nfeeds 2.7 mA into an input, 2.9 mA at tolerance\n(calculated). U22 and U23 do not invert.\nEach range gate has 100 k to ground, not to its\nsource: a gate-to-source resistor would bypass a\nshunt. Gate resistors: R102, R105 47 R, R108 10 R.\nC64 to C67 sit at pins 6 and 3 of their driver,\nC68 and C69 at the supply pins of U24."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.49 39.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "30c7de40-f1b7-5b45-8b0d-dc53f1a54588")
	)
	(text "Reset: every gate low, address 00, ladder at 0 V. The sequencer selects\nrange 3 before a mode switch closes. Range change: the gate of the next\nrange goes high with its address, the gate of the previous range goes\nlow after the overlap. A jump forces range 3: the sequencer has 100 ns\n(requirement), range 3 conducts 0.35 us after the threshold (simulated,\ntypical). Drop from the supply node to VOUT on a step from 1 uA to\n500 mA: 312 mV with 1 uF at the device, 169 mV with 10 uF (simulated,\nnominal); the limits are 0.5 V and 0.25 V (requirement).\nA current from VOUT back into the instrument gives no reading: it\npasses the body diodes of Q12 to Q14 and of the clamps until firmware\nselects range 3 and opens the output switch."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 195.58 36.83 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3332c039-dd5a-5ef7-9a67-8f15705726a1")
	)
	(text "range 2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 147.828 133.604 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4e0fcba8-b82a-55c3-a59c-c01dd9273949")
	)
	(text "U24 passes both sense taps of the active shunt:\nchannel 1 is range 0 ... channel 4 is range 3.\nAddress: R95 and R91 select range 0 while the controller\nis absent or in reset (120 uA of pad leakage, typical in\nthe RP2350 datasheet, give 0.61 V: below the 0.8 V low\nlevel; calculated). R112 and R111 limit the pin current.\nEN is pulled up to +12V_A, the supply of U24 (R113),\nso it never stands above VDD."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 213.36 72.39 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "962143a8-5095-5afa-b826-b3c3f5191169")
	)
	(text "Ladder clamp Q10, Q11: gate on drain through\n22 R, source on VOUT_S. Off below the threshold\n(datasheet: 1.3 V to 2.3 V; 0.45 A at 2.5 V and\n10 A at 3.5 V from its curve). In a hot plug or\na short they carry the surge until range 3\nconducts: simulated 8.8 A each, 14.2 A in one\npart with the thresholds at opposite limits;\nrating 21 A pulsed. A charged device on a lower\noutput discharges through their body diodes:\n12.5 A each at most (estimate).\nR90: idle level 0 V and bias return of the\namplifier. It is ahead of the shunts: its 50 uA\nat 5 V (calculated) are not part of the reading."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.59 123.19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cdc1d52c-a2dc-5760-aa5b-0209262e4d18")
	)
	(text "range 3"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 180.848 133.604 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d3e4e2ba-1899-5ea3-bd14-dbff2d2d5164")
	)
	(text "range 0"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 89.408 133.604 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d5a7a5e8-da20-5ee6-84f2-0df02817bbba")
	)
	(text "range 1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 110.998 133.604 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "df3b12c1-fe04-5a9e-a6c0-5823ff7c965a")
	)
	(text "Range 0: R101 1 k, always in circuit.  Range 1: R104 33 R.  Range 2: R107 1 R.\nRange 3: R110 0.1 R. A shunt drops about 100 mV at 100 uA, 3 mA, 100 mA and\n1 A (calculated). Q12, Q13 and Q14 switch one branch at a time on top of\nrange 0 and overlap during a range change.\nThe gain calibration of each range removes the shunt tolerance; the drift is\n25 ppm/K (R110: 50 ppm/K, datasheets). R107 is a two-terminal 1206 chip on\nthe four-pad Kelvin land: each end cap bridges the force pad and the sense\npad of its end. R110 is a four-terminal part. Ranges 0 and 1 share their\nforce and sense nets: route their sense tracks from the pads.\nLeakage budget across the ladder: 100 nA at 100 mV and 40 C (requirement);\nthe clamp type is a candidate."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 85.09 167.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "efe1e032-1a23-5848-b77e-05987d4b095d")
	)
